    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30865" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">neutrālis</span></b> , e, adj.
		neuter, in gram., of the gender of substantives, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>neuter</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">positio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 4, 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nomina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					1, 5, 54</span></i>
			 et saep.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">neutrālĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>as a neuter;</i> Gellius fora navium
			neutraliter dixit, <i><span class="en">Charis. p. 55</span></i>
		P.</div>
